title: Union Independence
card-image: img/cards/labor_rights.svg?v=2
subtitle: Fight for trade unions free of the state.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: soviet_affairs
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik' and labor_rights_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; labor_rights_timer = 3

Boris Batursky and the union men argue that unions must not become the state's instrument. The Bolsheviks say a workers' state needs no independent union to defend workers against it.

- @petition: Petition for the union's independence through the Soviet.
- @strike: Back a railway and printers' strike in defence of union rights.
- @compromise: Accept a compromise: the unions advise but do not oppose.
- @easy_discard

@petition
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, railway: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -3);
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 1, repression: 1});
!}

The Soviet debated the petition for a whole afternoon. It was rejected, but the union men noticed who supported it.

@strike

How should it be carried out? Phased in, with compensation and negotiation, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. By decree it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can pass it and enforce it against them.

- @strike_slow: Phase it in, with compensation and negotiation.
- @strike_decree: Pass it by decree, as written.
- @strike_force: Pass it by decree, and break any opposition by force.

@strike_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 6, railway: 6});
RO.add(Q, {bread: -3, repression: 5, soviet_democracy: 2, rel_bol: -4});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -4);
if (Q.legality > 1 && Q.repression >= 25) { Q.legality -= 1; }
});
!}

The railwaymen and printers stopped work for a day. The Cheka arrested several strike leaders, including two of our own. It was phased in slowly, with compensation where it was owed, and the opposition grumbled rather than raged.



@strike_decree
subtitle: The law as written. Its opponents will answer.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'decree', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 6, railway: 6});
RO.add(Q, {bread: -3, repression: 5, soviet_democracy: 2, rel_bol: -4});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -4);
if (Q.legality > 1 && Q.repression >= 25) { Q.legality -= 1; }
});
!}

The railwaymen and printers stopped work for a day. The Cheka arrested several strike leaders, including two of our own.



@strike_force
choose-if: strength >= 18
subtitle: Chance of breaking its opponents: Bolsheviks [+ odds_bol +]%. A camp under 45% is too strong to touch, and is left alone.
unavailable-subtitle: We lack the force and the allies to break the opposition.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'force', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 6, railway: 6});
RO.add(Q, {bread: -3, repression: 5, soviet_democracy: 2, rel_bol: -4});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -4);
if (Q.legality > 1 && Q.repression >= 25) { Q.legality -= 1; }
});
!}

The railwaymen and printers stopped work for a day. The Cheka arrested several strike leaders, including two of our own. [+ law_text +]

@compromise
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: -3, railway: -2});
RO.add(Q, {repression: -2, rel_bol: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', -2, 4);
!}

The union leaders accepted an advisory role. They will say it was the best they could get.
